Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||01-02-2001||03:33 AM||||where could i go to get a 4puck/6puck unsprung clutch? i think that those two sound to be what i want, but i have no idea where to get them. i know napa auto parts carries clutches, but performance ones like that? maybe a tuner shop? what should a clutch kit include, clutch, pressure plate, and throw out bearing? (sorry for all the questions, gotta get them all in while i have computer access) what kinda money should i be talking, and how hard is it to install the clutch (looking for recommendations. i have never dropped the cradle, but i figure i will just do that since theres a lot of stuff i need to do while the engine is out. thanks much for any responses! (btw, i am in oceanside, CA, if anyone knows of a particular place around there)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||01-02-2001||09:38 AM||||E-mail 1fst2m6. He had a 4-puck in his SE that he traded to GT Bastard. Said it was like a switch. Was either fully in or fully out. No take-up at all. If you tried to slip it at all, it chattered like hell. (Never drove the car. Just hearsay.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||01-02-2001||02:30 PM||||STETZ, a tuner shop probably won't be able to get it.  It's an ACT clutch, and they don't make one for the Fiero.  Travis gets them through Engineered Performance as a custom setup I believe.  It sounds like you haven't done much mechanical work...  If so, this might not be the clutch you want.  You need to change the way you drive stick and it puts extra stress on your drivetrain(it isn't easy on the flywheel and you'll likely snap some tranny mounts.)  And yes, it chatters like hell.  That's why I'm going with the less aggressive kush-lok setup.  It's shown on <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A>  as well.  You can order it directly from them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||01-02-2001||07:19 PM||||call George at the Fiero Shop - 510-233-4376 -- he can help you with all you need......the shop is in Richmond, CA......||||reg||1
